---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Implementation, Onboarding & Enablement" current="/implementation-enablement/" description="Richard Allen's transferable experience in software migrations, onboarding, training, release support, documentation, system transitions, and enablement.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Implementation, Onboarding & Enablement</div><h1>Help people adopt change with less friction.</h1><p class="lede">My experience is strongest where implementation connects customers, support teams, documentation, training, software change, systems transitions, and day-to-day adoption.</p></div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="change-journey" aria-label="Change enablement approach">
    <div class="journey-node accent-teal"><span>01</span><strong>Prepare</strong><small>Explain the change early and identify what people need to learn.</small></div>
    <div class="journey-connector"></div>
    <div class="journey-node accent-blue"><span>02</span><strong>Coordinate</strong><small>Connect customers, support, technical teams, and documentation.</small></div>
    <div class="journey-connector"></div>
    <div class="journey-node accent-gold"><span>03</span><strong>Launch</strong><small>Provide go-live coverage, troubleshooting, and practical guidance.</small></div>
    <div class="journey-connector"></div>
    <div class="journey-node accent-violet"><span>04</span><strong>Reinforce</strong><small>Keep training, documentation, and support going after release day.</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="proof-ribbon"><span><strong>6 months</strong> advance communication in a major HawkSoft software change</span><span><strong>Biweekly</strong> developer/staff coordination in the final two months</span><span><strong>Ongoing</strong> training after go-live</span></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Change made usable</div><h2>Implementation work from the user side.</h2></div><p class="section-note">The common thread is helping people understand, adopt, and successfully use changing systems.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">MOVE</div><h3>Customer database migrations</h3><p>Coordinated customer database moves between local environments and HawkSoft Online, helping customers navigate the technical and workflow transition while keeping communication and support connected.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">GO</div><h3>Major software release support</h3><p>Supported a significant HawkSoft accounting-system change through six months of advance communication, recurring developer and support coordination before release, extra launch coverage, and continued training afterward.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">TRAIN</div><h3>Training & enablement</h3><p>Trained customers and staff on software workflows, troubleshooting, product changes, features, and best practices; also created training documentation, presentations, webinars, onboarding materials, SOPs, and customer-facing instructions.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">DOC</div><h3>Product & process documentation</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, created training documentation, presentations, webinars, online content, and customer communications to support product understanding and customer experience.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">BILL</div><h3>Billing-system transition</h3><p>At Willamette Broadband, supported the transition to a new billing system while continuing customer service, billing, scheduling, troubleshooting, complaint resolution, and customer training.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">SCAN</div><h3>Earlier system-change experience</h3><p>At Shady Grove Adventist Hospital, helped with a tracking-system change and the process used to organize and digitize X-ray film records. The experience reinforced the importance of practical procedures during technology transitions.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><strong>Scope note:</strong> this page describes source-supported migration coordination, release support, training, documentation, onboarding, and systems-change experience. It does not claim formal UAT ownership, product-roadmap ownership, or a dedicated Implementation Manager title.</div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
